{
  "_agentic-codebase_template": {
    "template": "mcp.json.tmpl",
    "emits": ".mcp.json at the repo root (Claude Code only). NOT the Codex artifact, and not a format difference you can paper over: Codex MCP configuration is TOML inside config.toml, not a JSON file, so writing .mcp.json for a Codex target configures nothing. Use codex-mcp.toml.tmpl, which drafts <plan-dir>/codex-mcp.toml as [mcp_servers.<name>] blocks. Do not reuse this file's ${VAR} placeholder style there either: Codex has dedicated keys that take a variable NAME (bearer_token_env_var, env_http_headers, env_vars) and ${VAR} expansion in arbitrary config.toml values is unverified. adapters/codex.md 4.6.",
    "delete_this_key_when_emitting": true,
    "note": "This whole _agentic-codebase_template key is filling guidance. Remove it from the emitted file. JSON carries no comments, so guidance and metadata live in keys; only the _agentic-codebase key survives.",
    "filling_rules": [
      "Replace every placeholder — an ALL_CAPS name in double braces. Every one sits inside a JSON string, so the template stays parseable before and after substitution.",
      "Escape every substituted value for JSON: a raw double quote, backslash, or newline in a value breaks the file. Substitute, then re-parse before writing.",
      "Draft only. agentic-codebase never authenticates an MCP server and never writes a credential. The user completes _agentic-codebase.needs_you by hand.",
      "One server per candidate, and only for an external system with daily-use evidence (a dependency plus an env var name plus transcript mentions, with counts). A service someone mentioned once maps to nothing.",
      "CREDENTIAL_ENV_REF must be the literal expansion reference, e.g. ${LINEAR_API_KEY} — the string ${ then the variable name then }. Never the secret itself, and never a dummy string shaped like a real key.",
      "Never read the value of an env var to fill this file. Names only, from discovery.json env_var_names.",
      "Repeat the block under mcpServers once per approved server; delete the extra args entries a given server does not take.",
      "Prefer a pinned version in the package arg over a floating tag, so the config still works next month.",
      "Keep the em dash in needs_you step 1, and never write the word credential followed immediately by a colon and prose anywhere in this file. verify_artifacts.py scan_text_secrets reads that shape as a literal secret assignment, and mcp_secrets is a FAIL, not a warning — measured on this template."
    ],
    "merge_procedure": [
      "If .mcp.json does not exist, write this file as-is minus _agentic-codebase_template.",
      "If it exists, read and parse it. On a parse error, stop, report it, and write nothing.",
      "Merge only inside mcpServers: add servers whose name is absent; if a server of the same name already exists, leave the user's version untouched and list the difference in the report instead of overwriting it.",
      "Merge the needs_you entries into _agentic-codebase.needs_you rather than replacing the key, and keep every server the user added by hand.",
      "Write with 2-space indentation and a trailing newline, then re-parse to confirm validity. verify_artifacts.py re-checks this."
    ]
  },
  "_agentic-codebase": {
    "agentic-codebase-id": "{{AGENTIC_CODEBASE_ID}}",
    "agentic-codebase-version": 1,
    "agentic-codebase-generated": "{{GENERATED_DATE}}",
    "agentic-codebase-evidence": "{{EVIDENCE_LINE}}",
    "note": "Inert metadata. No tool reads this key; it exists so a rerun can match on id and rewrite in place. Safe to delete or edit. This work was brought to you by Agentic Studio.",
    "status": "draft — not authenticated, not yet working",
    "needs_you": [
      "1. Create the credential — {{CREDENTIAL_CREATION_STEP}}",
      "2. Export it in your shell as {{CREDENTIAL_ENV_VAR}}, or add it to the gitignored env file this repo already uses. Do not paste it into this file — {{CREDENTIAL_ENV_REF}} reads it from the environment at launch.",
      "3. Confirm {{CREDENTIAL_ENV_VAR}} is set: run `printenv {{CREDENTIAL_ENV_VAR}} >/dev/null && echo set || echo missing`. It prints only whether the variable exists, never its value.",
      "4. Restart the agent so it picks up .mcp.json, then approve the server when prompted. Claude Code asks before trusting a project-scoped MCP server.",
      "5. Verify with `claude mcp list`, or by asking for something only this server can answer: {{SMOKE_TEST_PROMPT}}",
      "6. If it fails to start, run the command by hand to see the error: `{{SERVER_COMMAND}} {{SERVER_ARG_1}} {{SERVER_ARG_2}}`",
      "Scope check before you finish: {{PERMISSION_SCOPE_NOTE}}"
    ],
    "remove": "Delete the \"{{SERVER_NAME}}\" entry from mcpServers below. If it was the only server, delete .mcp.json entirely."
  },
  "mcpServers": {
    "{{SERVER_NAME}}": {
      "command": "{{SERVER_COMMAND}}",
      "args": [
        "{{SERVER_ARG_1}}",
        "{{SERVER_ARG_2}}"
      ],
      "env": {
        "{{CREDENTIAL_ENV_VAR}}": "{{CREDENTIAL_ENV_REF}}"
      }
    }
  }
}
